  "query_preview": "..Abundant sunshine across the area today with high\npressure centered over Chihuahua MX/Texas Big Bend. As this high\nbuilds west and strengthens this week, the hottest high\ntemperatures of 2026 are in the forecast. HeatRisk across the\narea will range from Moderate to Major with very localized\nExtreme. Extreme Heat Warning in effect Tuesday and Wednesday\nfor portions eastern half of forecast area. A few locals, mainly\neast of Tucson, will see near record highs.\n\nSmall increase in moisture from the south this week will lead to\nlow end chance (10-20%) of afternoon thunderstorms along/near \nthe Intl border east of Nogales and eastern Cochise county. No \nsignificant influx of moisture is anticipated until after July \n2nd.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (June 30 to July 6)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (38-39% chance)\nPrecipitation: Leaning above normal (39-47% chance) mainly\nduring the July 2-6 period.",
